![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Saezo left you beneath the Trade Moon with his pumps deeply drinking in the endless influx of Spark from Ternus. Kaelith collected Axiom, the Eldimagus staff built to grow from focus to apprentice to equal, while the Lone Star emerged from its refit rebuilt in Inuran metamaterial and ready for a single catalyzation of its own.

Governor Rourke wanted the ancient disk back; Asha offered him amnesty instead. Then Xal Aran carried you to the Skull, took the disk into the Flame's keeping, and left Asha and Kaelith to confront Nara about the catalyst map that began all of this.

Nara admitted the map had been planted for you. The Web of Divinity showed almost every other path ending with your deaths on the Trade Moon, followed by every human and Inuran soul on Ternus being dragged into the moon to birth something that devoured all future possibility. Yet this path broke away: the freighter reached the dock, exploded, and bought the universe time. After Axiom received Ikadra's blessing and took Xal as his first Catalyst, you followed Nara into the Flame of Knowledge, past its silent berths and impossible archives and through the Swarm to ask the Web what had changed.

Now you stand on the Flame's bridge above the well of hot white fire of a Flame Catalyst, beneath a divine Web spun by the gods themselves that shows every choice still waiting to be made. Kek, its exhausted, insane guardian, has given the "shape" of an answer to you. Maena arranged the freighter and seeks the birth of their god. The Hand of Errata planted a weapon meant to corrupt the Spark supply before it reached the Trade Moon. Your interference made Saezo hesitate long enough for that weapon to find its target, but Maena remains tied to Spark's production and to something being mined beyond the Web, deep in the Umbral Depths. Stopping Maena or stopping Spark may close the hole, but Kek's last warning still hangs over the bridge of the Flame of Knowledge: Saezo **must** be kept calm. Even with the Hand's weapon in place, Ternus can still be lost if he goes through with his own plan to create a god.

![](https://app.roll20.net/users/avatar/266322/30)

Sshado C. (GM):--- Recap ---

OOC: Setting the current scene now

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The Flame of Knowledge bridge hangs over a well of white fire, its heat rolling across ancient controls strangled beneath glimmering, pale silk. Above you, the Web of Divinity stretches through impossible distances, each trembling strand carrying the ghost of a choice that might still be made. Millions of spiders remain motionless around the chamber, listening through every surface, while Nara stands beside you with her rifle lowered and her expression unusually sober. At the heart of it all, Kek braces his eight-limbed body against the temporal matrix, several exhausted eyes fixed on futures only he can see. His final warning settles into the silence between you: somewhere beyond this ship, Saezo still believes the Spark belongs to him, and for now, the survival of Ternus depends upon preserving that belief.

Xal Nara:"Aran is going to want to hear about this. No, this is a matter for the Pantheon. Which complicates the whole situation to a ridiculous degree. I don't want to drag you into our politics."

Kek:At that remark, Kek begins cackling madly.

"THE PANTHEON!!! O' THEY SHIVER IN THE LIGHT," he cries, reaching toward the web above him, limbs trembling in awe at whatever he sees.

Xal Nara:Nara is unfazed by this, looking lost in thought for the moment.

Asha Morrow:"Well.." Asha looks around the room absentmindedly for a moment as she processes further, "Maena needs to die, probably. Saezo needs......I don't know what to do with him other than string him along for the time being. Unless we find some solution to Spark that could evaporate the..._ocean_ of the stuff he owns, I have no idea what to do about that. The thought of being near the Trade Moon again knowing what we know makes me actually afraid."

Xal Nara:"Like standing on top of a big bomb."

Asha Morrow:"A future-devouring bomb, yes."

Xal Nara:That elicits a shiver from Nara. Too big of a concept.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"The only sure solution to the Spark is to ignite it. But that makes one damn big explosion. Probably big enough to destroy the Trade Moon and Ternus from the moon current location."

Xal Nara:"So Saezo is being played then, he thinks this is his project. It's Maena's from the start."

Asha Morrow:"Luckily I just added someone to my infinite crew who would love to see their end, or at least I think so. And she might know enough to get us somewhere with that."

Xal Nara:She perks up at that. "Do you think she could tell us where their facilities are?"

Asha Morrow:"I don't know the full extent of what she knows, but I wouldn't rule it out. Sure would make things easier at least. If nothing else she'll have a lead or two I'd bet. Better than nothing."

Xal Nara:"Okay. I'll try to keep the Pantheon out of your way. They won't be able to act right away anyway due to politics. But it's not going to be pretty. It's possible Shaya, Krox join Virkon against Ternus and Inura. What I don't want is for this to turn into war, but Ternus famously acts like dickheads when they're told no."

Asha Morrow:"Honestly if I'd known what Ternus was doing I'd have suggested letting Virkon eat them all."

Xal Nara:Nara nods at that.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"We are talking about stepping into a feud with an entire family line here. Are we prepared for that? Do we have the firepower to take on one of the oldest Inuran families alive."

Xal Nara:"Your advantage is probably that they don't know who you are. The moment I sneeze in their direction they aren't watching for you."

Asha Morrow:"This really isn't about if we can do this Kaelith, I don't think there's another choice that doesn't result in some new god being born which I think dealing with would be a little harder than with the Maenas."

"And anyways, this should be a step down for us from catalyst hunting. I imagine at least the first couple jobs for this will be a breath of fresh air comparatively."

"Unless I just jinxed us, but that would never happen - right Kek?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"No, no, no, I wasn't speaking of not doing it. I was merely stating that perhaps we need to rapidly prepare ourselves for this by equipping ourselves and your ship better."

Xal Nara:Something about what Asha just said cuts right through Nara's whole facade and for just a few moments you can see the young woman she was before she was drawn into this war and forced to become a Guardian. Her whole demeanor changes, "I didn't know you all were Catalyst hunters?"

Asha Morrow:"With what? We just went shopping at the biggest shopping center we know of."

Asha's face scrunches and she turns to Nara, "You..you planted a map of all the catalysts in the galaxy in a way that assured it would reach our hands, what did you expect us to do with it?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"And we have more catalysts to hunt. And **Yeah** you gave us the map." _Kaelith says with a twist of sarcasm in his voice_

Xal Nara:"I hadn't really thought about it like that before. You just reminded me of how I met Aran. We're all fellow Catalyst Hunters," she says, beaming. "I just think that's cool."

Asha Morrow:Asha smiles, any worry of where this is going falls off her shoulders "It is cool. With us you don't have to be a guardian you can just be Nara."

Xal Nara:Nara's shoulders drop a little and she nods at that confidently now. "Great. I'm kind of jealous to be honest. What Asha said about it being a breath of fresh air is right. You know, you spend like weeks or months drifting around in the Depths and then having these high intensity moments of life-threatening danger. If you forget the trade moon is a bomb then it's nothing compared to a Catalyst."

"Nothing beats some good old face to face infiltration on the surface of a planet is all I'm saying."

Asha Morrow:"There really is nothing like getting back at people who deserve it." Asha takes in a deep breath and looks around their surroundings again, taking in one last view "Alright the Captain in me is saying its time to fuck off, any more questions for our resident prisoner of the web?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Questions in this place are potentially dangerous. I'm good."

Xal Nara:Nara gives Kek a pitiful look and suddenly asks, "Hey. Kek, does _she_ have anything to contribute to all of this?"

Kek:Kek stares blankly back at Nara.

Xal Nara:"Okay," she says with a shrug. "Let's fuck off."

Asha Morrow:"Kek, you deserve better than this my friend. I wish you well."

Kek:"Thank you, Captain Asha. Please, I beg of you, never speak of what you found in this place."

Asha Morrow:"What place?"

Kek:Kek cackles at that and raises his eyes to the web.

Asha Morrow:She looks, "Nothing's there."

Xal Nara:"Must be the resting place of a hero, nothing more."

She waves to Kek and heads for the exit.

Asha Morrow:Asha follows quickly behind Nara.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith follows right behind_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Once they're all in step together, Nara simply blinks them back to the large flat area where the throne of Xal rests beside a large pool of black... something, probably blood pooled in the bone.

Xal Aran:Aran is caught staring off into space, just standing around on the flat dais of bone nearby. Voira is speaking quietly with Ikadra and then stops when you all snap into existence.

"Oh, that was fast. No trouble with the Swarm?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471386665/zJv8qeYHHUC9lyGAd4PC6g/med.png?1768350308)

Ikadra:"That place suuuuuuuuuuuuuuuucks," Ikadra rolls so low his 'voice' begins to crackle.

Asha Morrow:"That place does kinda suck, poor Kek."

Xal Aran:"Kek is the strongest among us."

"I don't really know why he hasn't died yet."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:"Mm, yes the last man who touched the web before Kek is still alive. He was cured, but it took the intervention of a Titan. That's how bad it is."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"He just went crazy instead. Dead is probably better."

Asha Morrow:"Remarkably sane for one in his position I'd say."

Xal Aran:"Strangely so."

"Regardless, do you have what you need? Do you need anything from Voria or myself?"

Asha Morrow:"I dunno, need to talk to my crew and figure out what we're doing next. Should be exciting. Kill or fuck some Maena or something I expect."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:"I actually have a gift for you, before you leave. Well, I had it transported to your ship. Your Sargent took control of it, but it's a barrel of revival brew from Drifter Rock. It can only do so much, but as long as someone just died and is mostly intact then it'll work."

Asha Morrow:"Well that's quite the gift, good for one use or?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:She does a little math in her head.

"If you are really careful, maybe a couple hundred brews in a barrel."

Asha Morrow:"Wow well that is a ridiculous gift then."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"That's a hell of a lot of reviving."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:She grins. "You have a fanclub among the Drifters. They love you two."

"Honestly, thank them."

Asha Morrow:"I certainly hope we don't need that much but safe is better than sorry in this...'business'?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:Voria takes a little too long to respond to that, doing the thousand yard stare. "Yeah, you never know. From one Captain to another, eventually you're going to lose someone and it's going to hurt. If I can stave that off for you a little longer then I'm glad to."

Asha Morrow:"I'll continue pretending my crew is immortal until reality is brutally shoved into my face, just like I did the last time one of my crew nearly died." She looks around at everyone and lands on Kaelith, "You need anything else here? I'm feeling that urge again that its time to fuck off."

Xal Aran:Aran chuckles at that.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471386665/zJv8qeYHHUC9lyGAd4PC6g/med.png?1768350308)

Ikadra:"Yeah why the fuck are you two still here?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:"You have got to work on your sarcasm Ikadra."

Asha Morrow:Asha gasps, "_Ikadra_ I thought we were friends?!"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I have gotten what I came for and we have gotten the direction of the Web, so I have nothing further. Fucking off is a good idea."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471386665/zJv8qeYHHUC9lyGAd4PC6g/med.png?1768350308)

Ikadra:Ikadra laughs at Asha's reaction.

Xal Aran:"All right, sending you off. Hold onto your lunch."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:You're just back on the bridge with a blink. It's all very weird and seamless as usual.

Asha Morrow:Asha clears her throat, adjusting for a moment before she projects her voice throughout the bridge "My dear crew its time to talk, gather round. We have some direction but first some of you need to find something better to do because we don't all need to be here for what comes next. I'm sure some of you may already have ideas on what else you could be doing so now is the time. Hands up who wants to fuck off for a bit and go off on a side quest?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Well. That was a tad fucking bizarre."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Violet light folds across the bridge, and Asha and Kaelith are simply there again, the last distortion of Aran’s translocation snapping shut behind them. The Lone Star feels almost offensively comfortable after the Flame, warm lights, clean consoles, familiar voices, and the quiet hum of newly rebuilt systems. Rho is seated at his station with diagnostics spread across three displays. Lysa and Yraina stand beneath a projection of the Skull and the two Great Ships hanging beside it, surrounded by manifests, sensor readings, and half-formed plans. Tamsin has claimed an auxiliary console as a workbench, pieces of a new Mark IX rifle arranged neatly around her. Seraphine is occupying the captain’s chair sideways, boots over one armrest. Nyrix is at the window staring out at the Skull of Xal. Every one of them looks toward you at once. Whatever casual business they were pretending to conduct stops. They have been waiting.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449881/cL_uCLa-CsHARMqCKTqirg/med.png?1769556779)

Rho Anselm:"I'm the XO, Cap. You're giving deets before I start agreeing to your wild plans."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:Lysa's hand shoots up. "Absolutely. Give me a mystery."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yrains "I have a route into Maena," Yraina says plainly, raising her hand reluctantly. "Calling it a side quest would be generous."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449929/F3ccik3dOgyO6n9WNHxu4A/med.png?1769556811)

Tamsin Vale:"If 'fuck off' includes field-testing this new hardware, game."

Seraphine Morrow:Seraphine is quiet, just listening.

Asha Morrow:"We need people in more places than one, I would consider getting into Maena the main quest right now they need to **DIE**." Asha exclaims dramatically, "But some of you need to find something else to do because keeping us all here is a fucking waste I can no longer tolerate, some of you are too talented to be wasting away on my bridge."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:Nyrix raises one hand. "I would like to accompany you if you are going somewhere _interesting_."

Asha Morrow:"Nyrix babygirl you stay, of course." Asha points out at Lysa, "Hold that thought I'll be back to you" she swings dramatically over to her mother, "Mother! **YOU** need to fuck off, you're a Ternus fucking major wasting away on my bridge while Ternus sends god creating juice into the trade moon, surely you could be doing something there to fuck with the flow of Spark or finding intelligence."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina crosses her arms and turns her chin up, the sheer Inuran arrogance coming out fully at Asha's declaration. There's a certain fire in her eyes now. "Glad we're on the same page."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:Nyrix lowers her hands, visibly pleased. "Good. I had already decided that was the correct answer."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449881/cL_uCLa-CsHARMqCKTqirg/med.png?1769556779)

Rho Anselm:Rho slowly leans away from the family confrontation. "For the record, I strongly support distributing our talent." He almost sounds sheepish.

Seraphine Morrow:Seraphine's boots drop from the armrest and she leans forward, grinning with unmistakable pride. "There she is. I was wondering how long it would take to get some real fucking orders." Her expression sharpens. "I'll go to Ternus, reactivate every contact who still owes Major Morrow a favor, and trace their procurement. Tamsin can come make sure I survive being officially unwelcomed."

Tamsin stops cleaning her rifle and glances toward Seraphine. “If the Major needs a bodyguard, I'm definitely a better shot than any of you on the bridge. No offfense."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"One would assume that you desire my services by your side, but that is your call Captain."

Asha Morrow:"Excellent!" her arm swings back to Lysa and she approaches her with big strides, "I need _more_, from everyone. And if you aren't going to join us on our assault on the Maena than you need to be doing something worth missing that. We have a catalyst map, we have Yraina who could give you another angle on hurting the Maena to support our main mission from the side, or perhaps you have your own idea on what you can do. I want to hear it."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:Lysa starts to say something, stops, then shifts a bit to lean on her staff. "Do you think Xal's faction would let us have access to the remains of Necrotis and her Great Ship?"

Asha Morrow:Asha tilts her head and _stares_ through Lysa, "That's quite the heretical question, somehow I love it. I **don't** think they would, yet I can't help but want to ask now. What the fuck would you do with that?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:Lysa smirks at the heretical remarks. "Maena's operation repeatedly uses Spirit magic and the last major source of that in the galaxy was the mage, Necrotis. It might be worth studying what was left behind on her ship to figure out what Maena must have learned from her.

"If not that, as much as I would love to go with you to the surface, it might be better for you to let me go spirit catalyst hunting with Rho. We are going to need someone who can break bindings, recognize them in the first place, and probably much worse."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"And I need to catalyze Axiom with her anyway."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:"You're not going to sub that one out for another?"

"Surely any other Spirit catalyst could work."

Asha Morrow:Asha sends a missive to Nara, "An officer of mine would like to study Necrotis' ship and her remains for help understand what Maena might have learned from them. Is this a no-go?"

"Yes, Kaelith as much as I want to support our resident fury of god on his journey having your staff catalyze with Necrotis is insane. I know that's the direction you were given but...ugh. Fuck."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449881/cL_uCLa-CsHARMqCKTqirg/med.png?1769556779)

Rho Anselm:"Assuming Kaelith and Lysa go to do... that. I have kind of an... out of the box kinda off the wall plan for you, Cap."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Why would I not take the opportunity to Catalyze Necrotis. If I must swap her out, i will."

Asha Morrow:"Music to my ears Rho, tell me more."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:"I think you should, Kaelith. Do you really want to make a staff with one imperfection?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Rho rubs the back of his neck, already looking faintly embarrassed. "All right. So, Saezo like us- or he likes paying us, which is close enough for Inurans."

Yraina points at that note and nods.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Orrel specified a specific order for catalyzation of Axiom. It may take some time to complete. I am supposed to go to Aashitak next."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449881/cL_uCLa-CsHARMqCKTqirg/med.png?1769556779)

Rho Anselm:He gestures vaguely, as if arranging the rest of the plan in the air. "We tell him Maena is making a move and offer him a platoon of heavily armed professionals to protect his precious Spark. Then, Smoke and I stand around looking all intimidating, learn where all the pipes go, and quietly find a way to make the really important ones stop working. Saezo gets to feel powerful, and if he panics then we could have a shot."

Asha Morrow:"Yeah I mean that does sound nice, but where do the rest of us come in for that?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449881/cL_uCLa-CsHARMqCKTqirg/med.png?1769556779)

Rho Anselm:"Well, if Lysa and Kaelith are going to visit Necrotis, and Seraphine and Tamsin are going to Ternus, then that leaves you and Yraina and Bell to start working the Maena angle.

"

"I guess that would make Smoke and I your inside job on the Saezo side."

"Again this is all just spitballing. Does anyone have a better idea?"

Asha Morrow:"Well I'm good with that but it sounds like Kaelith will not be doing Necrotis as he needs to stick to a certain order. So I guess he'd be with me. I'm good with it, not that picky about specifics at this point just happy to make some fucking progress in multiple places at the same time."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"So, I did say I have a way into Maena, but you're not going to like it."

Asha Morrow:"So you mean I'm going to love it, shoot."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina bites her lip and considers how to word this.

"We would need to steal a device from my old Matriarch for imprinting memory. It's magitech made for uh, probably torture, I don't know. You take an imprint before you wipe someone's memory so that you can restore it later. We make our backups, I wipe you and take you in. They rely on a lot of slaves. Once we're inside, I restore your memory... all good."

Asha Morrow:Asha leans over with her eyebrows raises as far as they go "So just kill me and bring a new me back to life in the body of old me, that is fucking _wild_ darling. Are all Inurans so absolutely out of their fucking minds?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"Don't be so dramatic, it's not like your memories are deleted. You just lose access for a bit."

Seraphine Morrow:"There is a risk of PTSD but that's usually only when you bring someone back from an extended wipe. A few hours would be relatively safe."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"How do they determine if someone is mind wiped? And would they scan another Inuran?"

Seraphine Morrow:"We should find alternatives first though, if the plan goes wrong then you're just fucked."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"It's pretty obvious, Kaelith."

"Doesn't matter how hard you try to act, you'll never be able to recreate the awe and confusion of a wipe."

